# Env files.
#
# `.env` holds PUBLIC client config only (EXPO_PUBLIC_* identifiers such as the
# Google OAuth web client id). It is committed on purpose: EAS builds from the
# git archive, so an untracked .env means those values are simply missing from
# the build. Never put a secret there - it would be committed with it. Secrets
# belong in EAS secrets (build time) or `firebase functions:secrets:set`
# (server side), and the local-only overrides below are never committed.
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env*.secret

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

example

# Firebase emulator logs
firestore-debug.log
firebase-debug.log
ui-debug.log

# Generated native projects (Expo prebuild / run:ios - app.json is the source of truth)
/ios
/android
.firebase/
